        "min": 12,
        "titulo": "How to ask questions",
        "explicacao": "Yes/no question: keep the sentence as it is and raise your voice at the end: «Ты студент?» There is no word-order inversion and no «do/does», and «есть» is not used. Answer: «Да.» or «Нет.» Question with a question word: put the word at the beginning: «Где ты живёшь?», «Когда ты работаешь?». The word «какой» agrees with the noun, like an adjective. To answer «почему», begin with «потому что».",
        "comparacao": "English can ask a question with intonation alone, too («You're a student?»), but only informally. In Russian this is the normal way to ask every yes/no question.",
